			}]
			x: -6.0d
			y: 1.5d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"bishop@romulus:~$ cat ch-001.jv"
				"Indentifier: ch-001 | Informal Name: Heart of Decay"
				"-------------------------------------------"
				"Subject ch-001 was delivered to the station hard frozen in ice until it could be moved to a secure lcoation."
				"Controlled durability tests showed thickened skin &lresistant to even diamond grade tools&r, though scans suggest it could be integrated technology."
				"In addition to its strong defense, one worker was spat at by a strange &lneurotoxin which seemed to slowly eat away at the his health. Active movement seemed to increase only its effect.&r"
			]
			id: "1121523438B3BF2B"
			rewards: [{
				id: "6C7A180895B0B76E"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 100
			}]
			tasks: [{
				icon: {
					Count: 1
					id: "ftbquests:custom_icon"
					tag: {
						Icon: "tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/icons/heart_of_decay.png"
					}
				}
				id: "767EA18EB3A517DB"
				observe_type: 5
				timer: 0L
				title: "Encounter a Heart of Decay"
				to_observe: "clanginghowl:heart_of_decay"
				type: "observation"
			}]
			title: "ch-001 \"Heart Of Decay\""
			x: -6.5d
			y: -7.0d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"bishop@romulus:~$ cat ch-002.jv"
				"Indentifier: ch-002 | Informal Name: Extraterrestrial Reaper"
				"-------------------------------------------"
				"Entering the lab, Dr. Carpenter was found slouched against the wall close by ch-001's containment. Further inspection revealed ch-001 had escaped and dug its way into Dr. Carpenter's chest. Fearing the worst, he requested he be contained until further tests could be performed."
				"Not long after his requested containment, Dr. Carpenter began convulsing. A matter of seconds later, he died as subject ch-002 emerged from within him."
				"Extra caution was taken during the following days. Testing revealed &lthe same resistant properties as ch-001&r."
				"The blade on the end of ch-002's arm appears highly sharp, much more so than the average sword. Test subjects attacked with it appeared to have large cuts that did not heal naturally, &las if it had temporarily lowered their maximum health&r."
				"Some are wondering if it may be possible to create something harnessable using the metal from subjects ch-001 and ch-002."
			]
			id: "0DD280488B9BE843"
			tasks: [{
				icon: {
					Count: 1
					id: "ftbquests:custom_icon"
					tag: {
						Icon: "tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/icons/extraterrestrial_reaper.png"
					}
				}
				id: "4836E7E956984E47"
				observe_type: 5
				timer: 0L
				title: "Encounter an Extraterrestrial Reaper"
				to_observe: "clanginghowl:extraterrestrial_reaper"
				type: "observation"
			}]
			title: "ch-002 \"Extraterrestrial Reaper\""
			x: -6.5d
			y: -6.0d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"bishop@romulus:~$ cat ch-003.jv"
				"Indentifier: ch-003 | Informal Name: Flesh Maiden"
				"-------------------------------------------"
				"When presented with a captured zombie, ch-002 showed an odd shift in behavior. Initially hostile, it showed no malice towards the zombie after its initial attacks. Scans showed an infection in the undead, and soon after, ch-003 emerged from it."
				"Initial durability tests confirmed the same durability as its predecessors."
				"Completely hostile, ch-003 attempted to attack the team members with its arms. When that had no visible result, Dr. Weaver attempted a better look through the glass, only for ch-003 to &lstrike with what resembled a long whip-like tongue&r."
			]
			id: "1428DFC072CD4426"
			tasks: [{
				icon: {
					Count: 1
					id: "ftbquests:custom_icon"
					tag: {
						Icon: "tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/icons/flesh_maiden.png"
					}
				}
				id: "2A6D0A4C2D12F033"
				observe_type: 5
				timer: 0L
				title: "Encounter a Flesh Maiden"
				to_observe: "clanginghowl:flesh_maiden"
				type: "observation"
			}]
			title: "ch-003 \"Flesh Maiden\""
			x: -6.5d
			y: -5.0d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"bishop@romulus:~$ cat ext_stl_smp.jv"
				"------------------------------"
				"___Report Date: 1982-06-25___"
				"An unknown metal was taken from sites of meteor showers alongside small rocks and a living specimen. Analysis of small samples revealed a structure similar in shape to that of steel. Properties have yet to be fully analyzed. A larger sample may be required."
			]
			id: "74B74B738FDAA691"
			tasks: [{
				id: "3C3BC4D57CF547C1"
				item: "clanginghowl:piece_of_extraterrestrial_steel"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "ext_stl_smp.jv"
			x: -5.5d
			y: -7.0d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"bishop@romulus:~$ cat ch-004.jv"
				"Indentifier: ch-004 | Informal Name: Hematoma"
				"-------------------------------------------"
				"We were given a rather odd subject. A pig who had reportedly been infected by another ch-001. Already in containment, we watched it for changes. After enough time had passed, ch-004 emerged."
				"An odd subject next to its bretheren, ch-004 does not portray any substancial resistance to outside damage. It appears rather weak in comparison. Instead, chemical analysis shows a gas emitted by ch-004 that appears to attract animals and mobs towards it. What's interesting is that the gas causes hostility in those capable. It's almost as if this creature is meant to die."
				""
				"___Report Date: 1986-07-18___"
				"Previous theories proved true when ch-004 was killed by a captured skeleton. Upon its death, ch-004 exploded, relasing a splash of blood that came into contact with a researcher's wolf, infecting it, and giving birth to ch-005"
			]
			id: "7CF4BBE81E1A7D4A"
			tasks: [{
				icon: {
					Count: 1
					id: "ftbquests:custom_icon"
					tag: {
						Icon: "tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/icons/hematoma.png"
					}
				}
				id: "65128D432DC8A182"
				observe_type: 5
				timer: 0L
				title: "Encounter a Hematoma"
				to_observe: "clanginghowl:hematoma"
				type: "observation"
			}]
			title: "ch-004 \"Hematoma\""
			x: -6.5d
			y: -4.0d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"kane@remus:~$ cat ch-005.jv"
				"Indentifier: ch-005 | Informal Name: Blood Spreader"
				"-------------------------------------------"
				"After being infected during an accident with ch-004, Dr. ███'s pet wolf was infected. Immediately following this, the wolf was quaranteened, and ch-005 later emerged."
				"ch-005 is more in line with the other subjects, showcasing a strong defense to traditional weaponry."
				"Dr. ███ fell into hysterics trying to get to the subject. His actions resulted in its escape, and the site was put into immediate lockdown. Following extraction showed the location itself greatly infected and in ruin. The large amounts of ch-002 and ch-003 were either captured or disposed of, and any natural lifeforms were put down."
				"Reviewed security footage showed ch-005 attacking researchers, often retreating after each attack before returning. Reviewers noticed that &lwhen it attacked or took damage, ch-005 released what appeared to be blood clots.&r After a small collection had been left and not destroyed, &lit howled and the clots took on a life of their own as copies of the original&r. Designated ch-005-1, these copies were weaker than the original, but also showed the ability to leave blood clots, though it was unable to create more ch-005-1. &lThe ability seems to only be present in the original cs-005.&r"
			]
			id: "5B76548804FFB620"
			tasks: [{
				icon: {
					Count: 1
					id: "ftbquests:custom_icon"
					tag: {
						Icon: "tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/icons/blood_spreader.png"
					}
				}
				id: "55EC78A5237C09FC"
				observe_type: 5
				timer: 0L
				title: "Encounter a Blood Spreader"
				to_observe: "clanginghowl:blood_spreader"
				type: "observation"
			}]
			title: "ch-005 \"Blood Spreader\""
			x: -6.5d
			y: -3.0d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"kane@remus:~$ cat ch-006.jv"
				"Indentifier: ch-006 | Informal Name: Prowler"
				"-------------------------------------------"
				"At site Remus, researches managed to infect a horse through contact with a ch-001. It seemed to be curious, and that intelligence was shown when it had been thought to have escaped. Upon entering its containment, however, ch-006 revealed itself, &lhaving turned invisble to the naked eye&r, and struck a powerful blow to one of the armed researchers, &lseemingly reducing their armor's strength&r."
				"ch-006's body contains canisters with a substance similar to that of ch-001's projectiles, &lapplying the same neurotoxin effect to another when slashed with its claws or tail&r."
			]
			id: "708BF47743F07494"
			tasks: [{
				icon: {
					Count: 1
					id: "ftbquests:custom_icon"
					tag: {
						Icon: "tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/icons/prowler.png"
					}
				}
				id: "4072DAE8F5088AE7"
				observe_type: 5
				timer: 0L
				title: "Encounter a Prowler"
				to_observe: "clanginghowl:prowler"
				type: "observation"
			}]
			title: "ch-006 \"Prowler\""
			x: -6.5d
			y: -2.0d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"kane@remus:~$ cat ch-007.jv"
				"Indentifier: ch-007 | Informal Name: Carcass"
				"-------------------------------------------"
				"After infecting a polar bear at site Remus, the resulting ch-007 showed to be passive at first. Unlike its cousin, ch-006, ch-007 did not outright attack researchers. Instead, it showed interest in infection, &lattempting to cover other creatures with a large volley of what appeared to be blood&r. When this did not work, or when presented with something immune to infection, its projectiles &ltook on a new, more directly dangerous form&r."
				"Over time, researchers began to notice growth in ch-007. While not immediately noticed, the timing was shown to line up with the deaths of other subjects. It appeared that &lwhen a technoflesh creature died near ch-007, it would increase in size and strength&r."
			]
			id: "47932CAA0EC704F4"
			tasks: [{
				icon: {
					Count: 1
					id: "ftbquests:custom_icon"
					tag: {
						Icon: "tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/icons/carcass.png"
					}
				}
				id: "087FEFD328A1F989"
				observe_type: 5
				timer: 0L
				title: "Encounter a Carcass"
				to_observe: "clanginghowl:carcass"
				type: "observation"
			}]
			title: "ch-007 \"Carcass\""
			x: -6.5d
			y: -1.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["74B74B738FDAA691"]
			description: [
				"bishop@romulus:~$ cat ext_stl.jv"
				"------------------------------"
				"A rather large sample of the unknown metal was brought in to be investigated. Research showed more similarities to our own steel ore, however its structure does not appear to resemble an alloy of any kind known to us. We expect more samples in the future as more meteor showers occur."
			]
			id: "39F18BD5E09298CE"
			tasks: [{
				id: "67C34BF01EC577C4"
